(Stage 1e2 review — the list printer's MAP branch. map.asm dispatches the
 LIST tag into _list_print, but list.asm had no matching MAP branch, so a
 map stored in a list slot fell through to the integer path and printed as
 a raw pointer.
 Was also a mixed map/list cycle test (c1/c2 referencing each other across
 types, hitting the shared depth budget and flagging an error).
 docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #111 (owner ruling, GitHub #34, Option 1): a
 collection placed inside another collection is now a COPY, so `set c1's
 "to_list" to c2` copies c2's state at that moment (empty), and the LATER
 `append c1 to c2` only changes c2 - c1's own "to_list" copy, already
 made, is untouched. No cycle forms and no error is set.)

a map called inner is {}.
set inner's "deep" to 5.
a list called holder is [].
append 1 to holder.
append inner to holder.
print holder.
If element 2 of holder is a map, print "elem2 is map".
Otherwise print "elem2 not map".

a map called c1 is {}.
a list called c2 is [].
set c1's "to_list" to c2.
append c1 to c2.
print c1.
on error print "mixed-cycle-flagged".
